# NPM Authentication Template
# Copy this file to .npmrc and replace YOUR_NPM_TOKEN_HERE with your actual token
# NEVER commit the .npmrc file with your actual token!
#
# To get your NPM token:
# 1. Log in to npmjs.com
# 2. Go to Access Tokens in your account settings
# 3. Generate a new token (Automation type recommended for CI/CD)
#
# For GitHub Codespaces:
# - Add NPM_TOKEN as a Codespaces secret in your repository settings
# - The devcontainer will automatically use it
#
# For local development:
# - Set the NPM_TOKEN environment variable, or
# - Copy this file to .npmrc and add your token directly

//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=YOUR_NPM_TOKEN_HERE

# Alternative: Use environment variable (recommended for CI/CD)
# //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
